# libsystemd0 (>= 258) is also implied by ${shlibs:Depends} (dpkg-shlibdeps
# picks up the real per-symbol floor from the built binaries, e.g.
# "libsystemd0 (>= 258~rc1)"), but src/defused_proto.h's Varlink usage needing a
# systemd this recent is significant enough -- current Debian stable and
# Ubuntu LTS don't ship it yet -- to also spell out explicitly here rather
# than leave it implicit in a build-time-computed substvar. See README.md's
# Installation section.
#
# polkitd, not the older policykit-1 name: current Debian (trixie) dropped
# policykit-1 as an installable package entirely, and current Ubuntu (26.04)
# did the same -- verified with `apt-cache policy policykit-1 polkitd` in
# both. Every distro new enough to satisfy the libsystemd floor above also
# has polkitd.
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, libsystemd0 (>= 258), polkitd
Description: setuid-less replacement for fusermount3
 defused replaces libfuse's setuid-root fusermount3 helper with a
 socket-activated system service (listening on
 /run/defused/defused.sock) plus a fusermount3-compatible client
 binary that talks to it over a Unix domain socket.
 .
 Because the setuid-root binary is gone, FUSE mounts keep working
 under the no_new_privileges process flag used by sandboxing
 techniques such as seccomp-bpf and landlock, and the privilege to
 mount FUSE filesystems can be granted per-sandbox by bind-mounting
 the socket into a container's namespace instead of relying on
 /usr/bin placement.
